  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Collaboration Netherlands South Africa water conference</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Africa ranks as the 30th most water-scarce country, facing challenges in achieving water security due to limited technical skills and capacity. Addressing issues like wastewater treatment and flood risk reduction requires knowledge and innovation. Partnerships between South Africa and the Netherlands can help by fostering collaboration, introducing Dutch technologies, and creating an enabling environment for innovation and entrepreneurship in the water sector.In this project, the exchange between South Africa and Dutch stakeholders will be facilitated through a networking event linked to the IWA International Conference on Water Reclamation and Reuse, and the engagement with the Wetskills challenge.</narrative>
  </description>
